  "result": "I fixed it, and the full test suite passes with the change (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 expected failure).\n\nI hadn't written a plan file yet because my last message asked which kind of ordering you meant. So I tried more help output myself and found the problem: each option was listing its long name before its short name.\n\n```\n--zeta, -z     \u2192   -z, --zeta\n--help, -h     \u2192   -h, --help\n```\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` builds the \"-z, --zeta\" label for each option. It sorted the names by prefix length in reverse, so `--` names came before `-` names.\n\n**Fix:** I removed `reverse=True`, so short names come first. The order of the options themselves didn't change: they still follow the order you declare them, with `--help` last.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_help_lists_short_option_names_first` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. It declares the long name first and checks that help shows `-n, --name TEXT` and `-h, --help`. I didn't run it against the old code to watch it fail.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
